  "interpretation": "Original named type60 Skim Missile is launched by nearby type43 drone: the popped68-byte Core record is assigned type60, World position/orientation/scale/exclusion fields, WORD24=20 and WORD26=150. Original primary/secondary type60 entries83FE/840A route through the two platform wrappers to35FB4/35FC8; both call35FD0. WORD24 decrements before signed BMI: nonnegative values add50 to LONG worldY, negative phase sets24 toFFFF then moves toward player by signed LONG difference ASR2 and decrements26; a negative26 clears retirement/durability and flagbits2/3. Thus only this subtype owns climb_updates_remaining24 and pursuit_updates_remaining26. They are updater-invocation countdowns, not seconds/physical frames, and the original zero/negative boundaries remain. Bind subtype at existing three original updater/helper contracts and type60 constructor result, not every free-pool entry or all WorldObjects. Shared3715E computes unwrapped LONG object-minus-player deltas with callerD7 arithmetic shifts;3713A subtracts and3714C adds them to objectXYZ. Preserve original overflow, ASR counts, untouched axes/buffers and wrapper assumptions. No arbitrary-caller/type safety, complete indirect-entry proof, live missile encounter or new gameplay coverage.",
